- install antivirus and antispyware: Malicious software, e.g. viruses and spyware, are designed to gain unauthorized access to computers and data. Once installed, viruses can destroy data and slow down computers. They can even take over the computer and broadcast spam emails from user accounts. Spyware can monitor online activities, collect personal information or produce unwanted pop-up ads on web browsers. To prevent this, only download software from trusted websites. always use antivirus software to provide another layer of protection and is designed to scan computers and incoming email for viruses and delete them. Keeping software up to date will help protect against new malicious software.

