Spoofing is a technique used by cybercriminals to impersonate a trusted source in order to gain access to sensitive information or systems. This can be done through various methods, such as email spoofing, IP spoofing, or website spoofing. The goal of spoofing is to trick the victim into believing they are interacting with a legitimate entity, leading them to disclose personal information, click on malicious links, or download harmful software.

simple forged or spoofed emails have led to massive data breachs and can cause irreversible reputational damage.

