Private mode works by preventing the browser from storing information about the user’s browsing session. This includes cookies, temporary internet files, and browsing history. However, it does not make the user completely anonymous online, as internet service providers (ISPs), employers, and websites can still track user activity. additionally routers and other network devices can still log user activity, and gather information about the user’s browsing habits. Private mode is useful for preventing other users of the same device from seeing your browsing history, but it does not provide complete privacy or security online.

